If a patient receives a buprenorphine-treatment for an opioid-use-disorder and has an acute-pain then every clinician may consider a temporary-buprenorphine-dosing-frequency-increase for the patient.
If a clinician uses a temporary-buprenorphine-dosing-frequency-increase for a patient then the patient may receive 2 buprenorphine-administrations per 1 day.
